`--root proj=specs` with a `tags.yaml` and two-level tags: the root gets a tag tree page with
descendant-inclusive counts and one page per tag, the parent's page listing its child's record.

-- fixtures/cwd/specs/tags.yaml --
ops: Operating the service
ops:deploy: Shipping a build
-- fixtures/cwd/specs/rule/0001-tag-releases.md --
---
type: rule
title: Tag every release
summary: A release is a git tag.
status: accepted
reviewed: 2026-10-01
tags: [ops:deploy]
---

# Tag every release
-- fixtures/cwd/specs/rule/0002-page-on-call.md --
---
type: rule
title: Page the on-call
summary: Alerts page one person.
status: accepted
tags: [ops]
---

# Page the on-call
-- cmd --
booping specs site --root proj=specs
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
specs site: 1 roots, 2 records, 12 pages, 0 warnings -> specs-site
